## 4. B0 fault signature (Q01, Q03, Q05, Q09)

Every fault line of the phase (199, UART 12229..19612):
`qcom-iommu-ctx 1e24000.iommu-ctx: Unhandled context fault: fsr=0x40000202, iova=..., fsynr=0x23, cb=4`.
fsr 0x40000202 = SS (bit 30, stalled) | FORMAT=1 (bits 10:9, AArch32 LPAE) | TF (bit 1, translation fault);
fsynr 0x23 = PLVL=3 (bits 1:0, level-3 table) | PNU (bit 5), WNR=0 (read). `cb=` prints `ctx->asid` (4). The
handler writes FSR back and RESUME=TERMINATE per fault. `errors: 04000000` = MDP5 INTR bit 26 `INTF1_UNDER_RUN`
(`mdp5.xml:116`).

First IOVA 0x386000 = 0x2000 + 3 x (640 x 480 x 4) = 0x2000 + 3686400 = the end of the source's mapped dumb-buffer
extent. Note 3 x 640 x 480 x 4 == 1280 x 720 x 4, so 0x386000 is also the start of the destination's second
buffer; `iovas_vs_source_map`: 10/10 outside the source map. All 199 lines hit 13 IOVAs 0x386000..0x386600 step
0x80, i.e. one 4 KiB page.

