## 7. Cold control (Q11): probe-time TLBIALL + TLBSYNC on all 5 banks from a cold SMMU

Facts:
- apq8016-sbc DT (built DTB, dtc): apps_iommu@1ef0000 ctx@3000 `qcom,msm-iommu-v1-sec` (camss), ctx@4000
  `-v1-ns` (MDP), ctx@5000 `-v1-sec` (venus); gpu_iommu@1f08000 ctx@1000, ctx@2000 `-v1-ns` (gpu). No
  `power-domains` on either IOMMU node.
- `ctx->secured_ctx` is set only for `qcom,msm-iommu-v2-sec` (source; objdump: `of_device_is_compatible()` with
  `.rodata.str1.8+0xb0` = "qcom,msm-iommu-v2-sec"). On MSM8916 therefore all 5 banks, including the two TZ-owned
  v1-sec ones, execute FSR clear + TLBIALL + sync at probe. (The commit message's "Secured contexts ... are skipped"
  is about v2-sec; it does not apply here.)
- `qcom_scm_restore_sec_cfg()` call sites in P: `qcom_iommu_init_domain()` (first attach per bank) and
  `qcom_iommu_resume()` only `if (dev->pm_domain)`. ctx probe runs from `devm_of_platform_populate()` before
  `iommu_device_register()`, i.e. before any attach. Inference: with no power-domains, this kernel's first
  restore_sec_cfg per bank comes after that bank's TLBIALL.
- Q11 (P FIT, relay pulse -> U-Boot -> bootm, UART 19176..19612, cold-dmesg 289 lines): pass=true, verdict CLEAN,
  mode `"640x480": 60 25175`, crtc active=1, 6 mapped vmas (3 x 1228800 B), cpus 0-3; `iommu sec: pgtable size:
  94208` 19498 (0.919015) with no `already initialised` line (first-boot SCM path succeeded), groups 0..3
  19499..19502 (0.924623/0.929133/0.936664/0.968523), Initialized msm 19602 (1.625308), 1 underrun (19610),
